          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong (combinatorial) species
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categorical
            presheaf on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+groupoid"} permutation groupoid
          %p
            A species is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+sequence"} symmetric sequence
            by another name. Meaning: they are categorically equivalent notions.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#1categorical 1-categorical
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %strong species
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Species
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Species := PSh(core(FinSet))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℙ
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P} := core(FinSet)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat \mathbb{P} := PSh(core(FinSet))
                  \\,.
          %p
            For more, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+type"} structure type
          %h3#2categorical 2-categorical
          %p
            A
            %strong 2-species
            (usually called a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff+type"} stuff type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-presheaf"} 2-presheaf
            on
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  core(FinSet) \to Grpd
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
          %h3#categorical
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-categorical
          %p
            Generally, an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-species
            or
            %strong homotopical species
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(FinSet)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  core(FinSet)^{op} \to \infty Grpd
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (
            %a{:href => "#GHK"}> Gepner-Haugseng-Kock 17, Def. 3.2.9
            ).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-species" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Species
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\infty Species := PSh_{(\infty,1)}(core(FinSet))
                  \\,,
          %p
            For more on this see also below the discussion
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#InHomotopyTypeTheory"} In homotopy type theory
          %h3#operations_on_species Operations on species
          %p There are in fact 5 important monoidal structures on the category of species.
          %h4#sum Sum
          %p
            The
            %strong sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + B
            of two species
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \coprod B
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            are computed objectwise, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A + B)_n \simeq A_n \coprod B_n
                  \\,.
          %p The generating function of the sum of species is the sum of their generating functions.
          %h4#cauchy_product Cauchy product
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(FinSet)
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            under disjoint union of finite sets. This monoidal structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (core(FinSet), \coprod)
            induces canonically the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            monoidal structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Species
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Species := PSh(core(FinSet))
            %strong Cauchy product
            of species, or sometimes (confusingly) just the “product”, since the generating function of the Cauchy product of species is the product of their generating functions.
          %p
            Explicitly, the Cauchy product of species
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi l
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi FinSet
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi l
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mi l
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo !
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo !
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mi l
                        %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A \otimes B)_n
                  \\simeq
                  \\int^{k,l \in FinSet}  A_k \times B_l \times Hom_{core(FinSet)}(n,k+l)
                  \\simeq
                  \\coprod_{k+l = n} \prod_{\frac{(k+l)!}{k! + l!}} (A_k \times B_l)
                  \\,.
          %h4#hadamard_product Hadamard product
          %p
            The category of species also has cartesian
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            are computed objectwise, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A \times B)_n \simeq A_n \times B_n
                  \\,.
          %p
            This operation is often called the
            %strong Hadamard product
            of species.
          %h4#dirichlet_product Dirichlet product
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(FinSet)
            also becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            under cartesian product of finite sets. This monoidal structure induces another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            monoidal structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Species
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Species := PSh(core(FinSet))
            = succeed "," do
              %strong arithmetic product
            %strong Dirichlet product
            of species, since the Dirichlet series of this product of species is the product of their Dirichlet series. (See
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/johnbaez/show/Dirichlet+species+and+the+Hasse-Weil+zeta+function"} Dirichlet series and the Hasse–Weil zeta function
          %h4#composition_product Composition product
          %p
            Finally, there is a monoidal structure on the category of species known as
            %strong plethysm
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong composition
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
          %h2#InHomotopyTypeTheory In Homotopy Type Theory
          %p
            The following discusses formalization of the concept of species in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hSet"} hSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            this automatically comes out as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of finite sets (see also at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+finite+types"} type of finite types
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
          #HoTTSpecies.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em species
              is a type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon Type
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi FinSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Species
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Species \coloneqq \sum_{X : Type} (X \to FinSet)
            %p
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi FinSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to FinSet
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              ranges over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+types"} type of types
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi FinSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  FinSet \longrightarrow {\|FinSet\|_{0}} \simeq \mathbb{N}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncation+modality"} 0-truncation modality
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+natural+numbers"} type of natural numbers
          %p
            Given a species
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi FinSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to FinSet
            as in def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoTTSpecies"}
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi card
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi FinSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f \circ card \colon X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} FinSet \to {\|FinSet\|_{0}} \simeq \mathbb{N}
          #HoTTGeneratinFunction.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+function"} generating function
              of a species
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi FinSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to FinSet
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoTTSpecies"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi fib
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi card
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi fib
                        %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Fin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi z
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|X|}(z)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} {\big| fib_{f \circ card}(n) \big|}\,  z^{n}
                    \=
                    \\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} {\big| fib_{f}(Fin(n)) \big|}\, \frac{z^{n}}{n!}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fib(-)
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin(n)
              denotes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-type"} 0-type
              with exactly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo :
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi : FinSet \to Type
              is a family of types, then we obtain the species
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo :
                        %mi FinSet
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi FinSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    pr_{1} : \bigg(\sum_{A : FinSet} \Phi(A)\bigg) \to FinSet
            %p with generating function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Fin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi z
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|\Phi|}(z)
                    \=
                    \\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} {|\Phi(Fin(n))|} \frac{z^{n}}{n!}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} stuff, structure, or property
              on finite sets, then we immediately know something about its generating function, considered as an exponential generating function:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi(A)
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Φ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Fin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi(Fin(n)) = 1
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+function"} exponential function
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{z}
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi(A)
                  is a family of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+propositions"} mere propositions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                  or
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  can be equipped with a
                  = succeed "-structure" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Φ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi(A)
                  is a family of sets (i.e., a
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+type"} structure type
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+natural+numbers"} type of natural numbers
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi(A)
                  has a higher homotopy level (i.e., is a
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff+type"} stuff type
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, \infty)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since any species
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Type
              is equal to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi fib
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    pr_{1} : \bigg(\sum_{x:X}fib_{f}(x)\bigg) \to Type
            %p
              every species is equal to one obtained from a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff+type"} stuff type
          %h3#operations_on_species_2 Operations on species
          %p
            The five monoidal structures mentioned above under
            %a{:href => "#operations_on_species"} Operations on species
            can be represented in HoTT, along with a couple other useful operations. We give four of the five monoidal structures here. For more operations, see (
            %a{:href => "#Dougherty15"}> Dougherty15
            ). We assume throughout this subsection that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Finset
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to \Finset
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Finset
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : Y \to Finset
            are two species, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo :
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi, \Psi : FinSet \to Type
            are two stuff types.
          %h4#coproduct Coproduct
          %p The recursion principle for the coproduct gives the species
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo +
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo +
                          %mi Y
                          %mo →
                          %mi Finset
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo +
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi rec
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo +
                              %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi FinSet
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi z
                          %mo ↦
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext if
                                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                    %mi z
                                    %mo ≡
                                    %mi inl
                                    %mi x
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi y
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext if
                                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                    %mi z
                                    %mo ≡
                                    %mi inr
                                    %mi y
                                    %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (f + g) &amp;:&amp; X + Y \to Finset \\
                  (f + g) &amp;:&amp; rec_{X + Y}(FinSet, f, g) = z \mapsto \left\{\array{ f(x) &amp; \text{if}\; z \equiv inl x \\ g(y) &amp; \text {if}\; z \equiv inr y .}\right.
                  }
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{A : FinSet} (\Phi(A) + \Psi(A))
          %p The generating function for the coproduct is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {|X + Y|}(z) = {|X|}(z) + {|Y|}(z)
          %h4#hadamard_product_2 Hadamard product
          %p The Hadamard product of species is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi FinSet
                          %mi Y
                          %mo →
                          %mi FinSet
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\langle X, Y \rangle &amp;:&amp; X \times_{FinSet} Y \to FinSet \\
                  \\langle X, Y \rangle &amp;:&amp; (x, y, p) \mapsto f(x)
                  }
          %p which for stuff types is equal to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi A
                              %mo :
                              %mi FinSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Φ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\sum_{A : FinSet} (\Phi(A) \times \Psi(A))
                  }
          %p The generating functions are related by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi n
                  %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {|\langle X, Y \rangle|}(z)
                  \=
                  \\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} n! X_{n} Y_{n} z^{n}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_{n}
            are the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X|}(z)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|Y|}(z)
          %p
            The name “Hadamard product” is used in (
            %a{:href => "#AguiarMahajan10"}> Aguiar-Mahajan10
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Bergeron08"}> Bergeron-Labelle-Leroux08
            ). In (
            %a{:href => "#Baez01"}> Baez-Dolan01
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\langle X, Y \rangle|}(1)
            is called the “inner product” of stuff types, because equipping the category of stuff types with this operation makes it a categorified version of the Hilbert space of a quantum harmonic oscillator.
          %h4#HoTTCauchyProduct Cauchy product
          #HoTTCauchyProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em Cauchy product
              of species is given by sending two species
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoTTSpecies"}
              to the species given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo :
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                            %mo →
                            %mi FinSet
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo :
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ↦
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (f \cdot g) &amp;:&amp; X \times Y \to FinSet \\
                    (f \cdot g) &amp;:&amp; (x, y) \mapsto f(x) + g(y)
                    }
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The Cauchy product, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoTTCauchyProduct"}
              %a{:href => "%28infinity,n%29-category+of+correspondences#PhasedTensorProduct"} phased tensor product
              on the slice over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              groupoid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (FinSet, \coprod)
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff+types"} stuff types
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoTTCauchyProduct"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo :
                        %mi FinSet
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo +
                        %mi V
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sum_{A, U, V : FinSet} \sum_{p : U + V = A} (\Phi(U) \times \Psi(V))
            %p
              In this form the Cauchy product is discussed in (
              %a{:href => "#AguiarMahajan10"}> Aguiar-Mahajan 10, def. 8.5
              ,
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#AguiarMahajan12"} Aguiar-Mahajan 12, section 2.2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} Monoids
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
              in the resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              of species are discussed in (
              %a{:href => "#AguiarMahajan10"}> Aguiar-Mahajan 10, section 8.2
              ) and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+monoids"} Hopf monoids
              in this category in (
              %a{:href => "#AguiarMahajan12"}> Aguiar-Mahajan 12, section 2.2
              ).
            %p
              This means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi\Psi
              stuff on a finite set is the stuff of “being chopped in two, with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              stuff on one part and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
              stuff on the other”.
            %p The generating function is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|X \cdot Y|}(z) = {|X|}(z) \cdot {|Y|}(z)
                    \\,.
          %h4#composition Composition
          %p The composition of two species is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mover
                            %mo ∘
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo :
                              %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi FinSet
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mover
                            %mo ∘
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↦
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi u
                              %mo :
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (f \tilde{\circ} g) &amp;:&amp; \bigg(\sum_{x:X}(f(x) \to Y)\bigg) \to FinSet \\
                  (f \tilde{\circ} g) &amp;:&amp; (x, p) \mapsto \sum_{u:f(x)}g(p(u)).
                  }
          %p For stuff types, this amounts to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi Fin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi card
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mrow
                      %mi card
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi Fin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi card
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{(A, C : FinSet)}\sum_{(B : Fin(card(C)) \to FinSet)} \bigg(
                  (B\vdash_{card(C)}A) \times \Phi(C) \times \prod_{k : Fin(card(C))} \Psi(B(k))
                  \\bigg)
          %p
            That is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mover
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi \tilde{\circ} \Psi
            stuff on a finite set is a partition of the set into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi card
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} card(C)
            subsets, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            stuff on the partition and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
            stuff on each of the subsets.
          %p The generating function of the composition is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {|X \tilde{\circ} Y|}(z) = {|X|}({|Y|}(z))
          %p
            This species is also called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plethysm"} plethysm
            product.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#cardinality Cardinality
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cardinality"} groupoid cardinality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi tame
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {|-|} : \infty Grpd_{tame} \to \mathbb{R}
          %p
            every (tame)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            is mapped to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \mapsto {|X|} := \sum_{[x] \in \pi_0(X)}\prod_{i = 1}^{\infty} (\pi_i(X,x)^{(-1)^{i}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            A species
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
            assigns an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_n
            to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cardinality"} groupoid cardinality
            we may naturally think of a tame species as mapping to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msup
                    %mi z
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{X} \mapsto {|\mathbf{X}|}
                  \:=
                  \\sum_{n = 0}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n!} {|\mathbf{X}_n|} z^n
                  \\in
                  \\mathbb{R}[ [ z ] ]
                  \\,.
          %p
            This cardinality operation maps the above addition and multiplication of combinatorial species to addition and multiplication of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
          %p
            That
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            of species maps to sum of their cardinalities is trivial. That
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            of species maps under cardinality to the product of their cardinality series depends a little bit more subtly on the combinatorial prefactors:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mi l
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                      %mi l
                      %mo !
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {| A \otimes B |}
                  \=
                  {|A|} \cdot {|B|}
                  \=
                  \\sum_{n=0}^\infty
                  \\frac{1}{n!}
                  \\sum_{k+l = n} \frac{n!}{k! l!}
                  {|A_k|} \cdot {|B_l|}
                  \\,.
          %h2#variants Variants
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If in the definition of combinatorial species the domain
                = succeed "(" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
                and also the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
                are take with values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
                then one obtains the notion of
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur+functor"} Schur functor
            %li
              %p
                Instead of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(FinSet)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} A
                for a small category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle a_i \rangle_{i \in I}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(FinSet)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                valued presheaves, we may consider those valued in presheaves on a small category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong generalised species
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+2-category"} cartesian closed 2-category
                (
                %a{:href => "#FGHW"}> FGHW
                ).
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of species goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Joyal81
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em Une théorie combinatoire des séries formelles
              , Advances in Mathematics 42:1-82 (1981)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0001-8708(81)90052-9"} doi
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=633783"} MR84d:05025
          %p An expository discussion can be found at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"}> Todd Trimble
              ,
              %em Exponential Generating Function and Introduction to Species
              (
              %a{:href => "http://topologicalmusings.wordpress.com/2009/03/28/number-of-idempotent-endofunctions/"}> blog
              ) (scroll down a bit).
          %p
            See also Wikipedia:
            %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combinatorial_species"} combinatorial species
            and
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                François Bergeron, Gilbert Labelle, Pierre Leroux,
                %em Théorie des espèces et combinatoire des structures arborescentes
                , LaCIM, Montréal (1994). English version:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Combinatorial+species+and+tree-like+structures"} Combinatorial species and tree-like structures
            %li#Bergeron08
              %p
                F. Bergeron, G. Labelle, P. Leroux,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to the Theory of Species of Structures
                %a{:href => "http://bergeron.math.uqam.ca/Site/bergeron_anglais_files/livre_combinatoire.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                François Bergeron,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Species and variations on the theme of species
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.itu.dk/research/theory/ctcs2004/"} Category Theory and Computer Science ‘04
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://bergeron.math.uqam.ca/Especes_trans.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                G. Labelle,
                %a{:href => "http://www.sms.cam.ac.uk/media/937;jsessionid=9540827CB40AC9F1E61BF944127EBAF4"} video
                intro into combinatorial species at Newton Institute, Cambridge 2008
            %li#AguiarMahajan10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Aguiar"}> Marcelo Aguiar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Swapneel+Mahajan"} Swapneel Mahajan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monoidal+Functors%2C+Species+and+Hopf+Algebras"} Monoidal Functors, Species and Hopf Algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"} Kenneth Brown
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Chase"} Stephen Chase
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
                %strong 29
                Amer. Math. Soc. 2010. lii+784 pp. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~maguiar/a.pdf"}> author pdf
                )
            %li#AguiarMahajan12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Aguiar"}> Marcelo Aguiar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Swapneel+Mahajan"} Swapneel Mahajan
                %em Hopf monoids in the category of species
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.3120"}> arXiv:1210.3120
                )
          %p
            The Dirichlet product of species seems to match what Maia and Méndez call the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong arithmetic product
          %ul
            %li
              Manuel Maia and Miguel Méndez, On the arithmetic product of combinatorial species,
              %em Discrete Mathematics
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 308
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0012365X07007960"} web
          %p An application in computer science:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brent+Yorgey"}> Brent Yorgey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Random testing and beyond! with combinatorial species
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~byorgey/talks/combtesting-ku-20091124.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %em Species and functors and types, oh my
              %a{:href => "http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~byorgey/papers/species-pearl.pdf"} pdf
          %p Homotopical species are defined in (Def. 3.2.9):
          %ul
            %li#GHK
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Joachim Kock
              = succeed "," do
                %em ∞-Operads as Analytic Monads
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06469"} arXiv:1712.06469
          %p
            Formalization in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brent+Yorgey"}> Brent Yorgey
                ,
                %em Combinatorial Species and labelled structures.
                (
                %a{:href => "http://ozark.hendrix.edu/~yorgey/pub/thesis.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Dougherty15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Dougherty"}> John Dougherty
                ,
                %em Species in HoTT
                (
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/jdoughertyii/hott-species/blob/master/species.pdf?raw=true"}> pdf
                ) (
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/jdoughertyii/hott-species"}> formalization in Coq
                )
          %p An application in statistical mechanics:
          %ul
            %li
              W. Faris,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Combinatorial species and cluster expansions
              = succeed ":4" do
                %strong 10
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/distribution/mmj/vol10-4-2010/faris.pdf"} pdf
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2791054"} MR2791054
          %p
            Discussion in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
          %ul
            %li#Baez01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dolan"} James Dolan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mathematics Unlimited - 2001 and Beyond
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0004133"} arXiv
          %p Discussion of generalised species:
          %ul
            %li#FGHW
              M. Fiore, N. Gambino, M. Hyland, G. Winskel,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The cartesian closed bicategory of generalised species of structures
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www1.maths.leeds.ac.uk/~pmtng/Publications/generalised-species.pdf"} pdf
